{"request_sha256": "903207490f0de299aa66e4f205d9d065e6d83847add757da9e6e0f05662adb2c", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "40a24923f1010ccc9178981b02415830b9daa76a0a1a47ce1a7b56c0e817f544", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 7021}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["crown-pinnate-arching-fronds: in both P-WHOLE renders the crown is a flat starburst of short, straight, nearly radial fronds; frond length is a small fraction of trunk length (roughly 1/6-1/7 of visible trunk in render-0/render-1) whereas reference-0 shows fronds whose length is a large fraction of the trunk and whose outline reads as a rounded shuttlecock. No frond descends below the crown base; the lowest fronds are horizontal or only slightly declined, versus the pronounced drooping skirt in reference-0 and the recurving lower fronds in reference-1.", "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow: leaflets render as tiny sparse dark ticks along a bare rachis (visible at scale in render-2), leaving the rachis line dominant and the frond translucent; reference-0/1/2 show densely packed, long, stiff linear-lanceolate leaflets that fill the frond and give a solid plumose blade. Leaflet size relative to frond length is far below reference.", "owner-fronds-long-arching (owner priority 1): unresolved on both seeds. Fronds remain thin and short; no arching curvature and no drooping lowest fronds.", "owner-trunk-straight-constant (owner priority 2): the trunk carries a distinct lateral kink/S-jog in the upper third immediately below the crown in render-0 and render-2, and a shallower but still visible jog in render-1; the profile is wavy rather than straight or gently leaning.", "solitary-columnar-stem / near-constant diameter: the trunk tapers markedly from a flared wide base to a narrow apex in render-0, render-1 and render-2, instead of the near-constant column of reference-0/1/2.", "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern: the drawn trunk is a smooth untextured tapering cylinder in render-0, render-1 and render-2; no leaf-base stubs or spiral lattice are present, against the coarse diamond/rhomboid stub tessellation covering the trunk in reference-1 and reference-2 and the knobbly texture at distance in reference-0. The owner has deferred the trunk organs (fn-110), but the trait is core and its absence is observed, not unassessable.", "trunk-fibrous-matting: no fibre or shredded husk is drawn anywhere on the trunk in render-0/1/2, against the packed reddish-brown matting filling the stub interstices in reference-1 and reference-2. Same deferral note as above.", "fruit-clusters-pendent: no inflorescence or fruiting bunch is drawn in either P-WHOLE render, against the two-to-three pendent orange-red bunches in reference-0. Owner has deferred the date cluster (fn-111); recorded as an observed absence of a core reference trait, not dismissed.", "leaf-base-close (P-BASE, render-3): the frame is an extreme close-up in which the subject fills the width and the left ~55% is crushed to near-black; no surface structure is resolvable. Input metadata also marks this render's visibility as hidden. Unknown on evidence grounds rather than fail.", "Finish quality: leaflet billboards in render-2 show hard black unlit facets mixed with lit green ones across the crown, reading as flat shading/backface artefacts rather than the coherent needle mass of the fn9 spruce anchor (anchor-0). Recorded against the finish floor only, not morphology."], "observations": ["Both P-WHOLE seeds (render-0, render-1) agree on every defining reading: same starburst crown, same taper, same upper-trunk jog. The two seeds differ only in the severity of the kink and slight frond count; no seed shows the reference character.", "The trunk is bare of epiphytes, vines and any foliage in render-0 and render-1, matching the owner's third priority. The epiphytic ferns in reference-1/reference-2 are scene features recorded as variation in the inventory and are correctly not reproduced.", "The stem is single and unbranched in all renders, which is the one half of solitary-columnar-stem that is supported; the constant-diameter half is not.", "Frond count in the crown is roughly 25-35 in render-0/render-1, inside the inventory's stated 30-60 range at the low end; count is not the failing dimension, frond length and leaflet size are.", "No dead-frond skirt (secondary) is drawn; reference-0 shows a brown collar beneath the living crown. Not scored as a core cell.", "No crownshaft is drawn, which is consistent with crown-shaft-absent in reference-1, though with a bare smooth trunk the absence carries little weight.", "frond-colour-range: the mid-to-deep green of the rendered leaflets sits inside the range spanned by reference-0 (deep green) and reference-1/2 (grey-glaucous); no finding either way.", "trunk-lean-and-curve is recorded in the inventory as variation spanning a strong S-curve (reference-0) to vertical (reference-1/2); the render's defect is not lean but a localised wavy jog with taper, which the owner has explicitly ruled out regardless of that variation band.", "The P-BASE cell was requested at close range for a trait the generator does not yet express; the framing delivered makes even the drawn smooth surface unassessable.", "Relative to any earlier state, the crown now reads as a single apical rosette on an unbranched stem, but that is not absolute readiness against the reference-only inventory."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown is a flat radial starburst of short straight fronds with no arching and no fronds drooping below the crown base, in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with frond length and leaflet size dials being set far below the reference, and with no gravity-driven droop applied to older fronds; the mechanism is not established by the images."}, {"observation": "Leaflets are sparse short ticks on a visible bare rachis rather than a dense stiff blade.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with the owner's reading that leaflet size is a primary dial; not established."}, {"observation": "Trunk shows a lateral kink below the crown and a pronounced base-to-apex taper.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The host note records the palm's taper value of 1.0 as outside the authored 0.05-0.6 range and as where the owner wants the trunk; consistent with the observed taper, but the kink's origin is not determined from the renders."}, {"observation": "Trunk surface carries no leaf-base stubs, no spiral lattice and no fibrous matting.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states the trunk organs (fn-110) are not landed in this pass; the absence is observed regardless of cause."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruiting bunches are drawn.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states the date cluster (fn-111) is not landed in this pass."}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk in either P-WHOLE seed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "A single unbranched stem carries the crown at a single apical point.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "P-BASE frame is an unresolvable extreme close-up, largely crushed to black, and is flagged hidden in the inputs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with a camera-distance or framing fault for this view; the metadata visibility flag is a separate candidate. Neither is established."}, {"observation": "Leaflet cards alternate between lit green and fully black facets across the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "anchor-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with single-sided or unshaded leaflet billboards; not established. Scored against the anchor's finish floor only, never its morphology."}, {"observation": "Foliage hue sits within the green-to-glaucous span the references themselves disagree on.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Trunk lean/curve is recorded as variation in the references, but the render's wavy jog is outside the owner's stated requirement rather than inside that band.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No dead-frond skirt beneath the crown (secondary priority).", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Fronds are short, straight and radial with no arching descent; the crown outline is a flat star, not the rounded shuttlecock of reference-0. Defining mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Leaflets are sparse minimal ticks leaving the rachis exposed; references show dense stiff linear-lanceolate leaflets filling a plumose blade. Defining mismatch, not a finish-quality issue."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Trunk is drawn as a smooth cylinder over its whole visible length at two scales; the stub lattice is observably absent, not merely unresolved. Owner has deferred fn-110, which explains but does not resolve it."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No fibre or husk anywhere on the drawn trunk. Observed absence of a core reference trait; deferred by the owner, recorded not dismissed."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Unbranched and single: supported. Roughly constant diameter: not met, the stem tapers strongly from a flared base to a narrow apex and jogs laterally. The trait as stated in the inventory includes constant diameter, so the cell fails."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "No pendent bunches drawn in either seed where the crown is fully visible. Owner defers the date cluster to fn-111; reported as an observed absence of a core trait."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary. No brown collar of collapsed dead fronds beneath the living crown; the crown-to-trunk transition is abrupt and bare."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait. Rendered green falls within the deep-green to grey-glaucous span the references themselves disagree on; acceptable variation."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. The crown centre in render-2 is a dark congested mass of overlapping leaflet cards; petiole bases and any sheath colouring are not resolvable."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait spanning leaning-S-curved to vertical, but the render's localised wavy kink below the crown is a different shape from either reference posture and is explicitly excluded by the owner's second priority."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, absent in reference-0 and present in reference-1/2 as a scene feature. Bare trunk in the render is within the observed range and matches the owner's third priority."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary. Trunk renders as a flat dark grey-brown with a single smooth gradient and no weathering, no lighter bleached stub faces, no warm reddish fibre tones; render-3 is largely crushed to black. Mismatch against the varied weathered surface of all three references."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-3", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary and marked uncertain in the inventory itself. The render shows a widening at ground level, but the reference observation is unresolvable at reference-0's scale, so the comparison cannot be made either way."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. No smooth green columnar sheath sits between crown and trunk in render-2; frond bases meet the trunk directly, as in reference-1. Weak support given the trunk is otherwise featureless."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary and flagged uncertain in the inventory. Proximal frond regions in the render are inside the congested dark crown centre; neither presence nor absence of spine-like reduced leaflets is assessable."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Variation trait with ratios the inventory says cannot be measured precisely, but the render is outside any plausible reading of it: crown spread is a small fraction of trunk height and frond length is a small fraction of trunk length, where reference-0 shows a crown of comparable scale to the trunk."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"c35abf8a-e388-43ae-9d06-b8cce8152a6a","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename"